Yes. But at that point, you have about ten seconds' involvement with
that character. That's not the same thing.
I remember adventure games where, in the endgame, you didn't get to win
unless you had, for no earthly reason, picked up a certain object or
pushed a certain switch, very early in the game - and of course by now
it was too late to return, and _all_ your saved games were useless
because you had, innocently, not done that one thing. Those games were
deleted very rapidly thereafter. 
Killing your game off soon after the start is acceptable. Doing it
because of something _you_ did is very acceptable. Making your game a
tedious slog because the RNG has repeatedly come up with zeroes needs
remedying, and that's what things like /oW and magic markers are for.
You can probably afford to strongly curtail either or the other, but not
both.

